{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_37","type":"reasoning","text":"Marker resolution worked out. All organs have 6+ marker symbols. Next, step 2: stream-process the count table and accumulate promoter/flank counts for these marker genes.\n\nNote: HOX genes were found (HOXA13, HOXD10/11/13, HOXC10/13, HOXB13 — probably plain tokens). INS, GCG, SFTPC, TNNT2, NKX2-1, NKX3-1, NKX6-1, SLC12A1, APOB are resolved.\n\nWait — for the Limb, HOXA9/10/11, HOXD9/12, etc. were missing, but HOXA13 and HOXD10/11/13 are present. 18 symbols were resolved. Good enough.\n\nNow, streaming. Sample order (columns): Bladder, Brain, Cloaca, GallBladder, Gill, Heart, Intestine, Kidney, Limb, Liver, Lung, Pancreas, Prostate, Spleen, Stomach.\n\nFor each gene g and each sample s, I need to write a streaming script that computes prom_counts[g][s], flank_counts[g][s], flank_bins[g], prom_bins[g], plus the per-sample column totals.\n"}}
