\n5. Also recompute all 105 pairs for the CSV: pairs not involving Stomach/Prostate → old scores (from the step 5 E matrix). Pairs involving Stomach or Prostate → recompute with the new rows.\n\nFrom step 5, I have the full old E matrix e(A→B) (15×15). Let me transcribe it (chunk b08ab9):\n\ne(A->B) rows (order: Bladder, Brain, Cloaca, GallBladder, Gill, Heart, Intestine, Kidney, Limb, Liver, Lung, Pancreas, Prostate, Spleen, Stomach):\nBladder:      --,-0.58,0.86,-1.08,0.72,-0.31,0.48,-0.26,-0.38,-0.55,-0.02,-0.67,0.27,-0.55,0.51\nBrain:        -1.68,--,-0.88,-2.34,-1.13,-1.28,-1.40,-1.90,-1.73,-1.94,-1.35,-1.75,-1.47,-1.61,-1.04\nCloaca:       -0.13,-0.20,--,-0.69,0.42,0.11,-0.12,-0.39,0.07,-0.48,-0.22,-0.74,0.06,-0.27,0.69\nGallBladder:  0.62,0.15,1.34,--,1.07,0.09,1.07,0.62,0.31,0.16,0.90,0.43,1.12,-0.20,0.87\nGill:         -0.38,-0.22,0.13,-0.87,--,-0.24,-0.13,-0.36,-0.52,-0.32,0.07,-0.61,-0.14,-0.27,0.06\nHeart:        -0.74,-0.99,-0.51,-1.72,-0.45,--,-0.80,-1.15,-0.67,-1.14,-0.67,-1.20,-0.95,-1.00,-0.57\nIntestine:    -1.21,-1.42,-0.73,-1.44,-0.87,-1.21,--,-1.27,-1.18,-1.32,-1.09,-1.48,-1.24,-1.57,-0.43\nKidney:       -1.04,-1.13,-1.16,-1.22,-1.10,-0.89,-1.23,--,-1.37,-1.24,-1.06,-0.99,-0.76,-1.49,-1.22\nLimb:         0.25,-0.33,0.25,-1.45,0.43,0.21,-0.08,-1.05,--,-0.66,0.06,-0.80,0.19,-0.52,0.56\nLiver:        -1.44,-1.59,-1.10,-1.35,-0.82,-1.29,-0.56,-0.86,-1.38,--,-1.18,-1.11,-1.32,-1.67,-0.94\nLung:         -1.01,-1.54,-0.54,-2.46,-0.47,-1.10,-1.03,-1.47,-1.31,-1.12,--,-1.65,-0.76,-1.46,-0.73\nPancreas:     -0.93,-0.64,-0.46,-1.27,-0.68,-1.20,-0.61,-0.98,-1.02,-0.98,-0.77,--,-1.07,-1.39,-0.69\nProstate:     0.10,-0.24,0.18,-1.09,0.34,-0.14,-0.14,-0.37,0.21,0.03,0.56,-0.57,--,-0.11,0.66\nSpleen:       -1.78,-2.08,-1.30,-2.52,-1.08,-0.89,-1.81,-1.80,-1.63,-1.19,-1.22,-1.95,-1.31,--,-1.28\nStomach:      0.66,0.48,0.62,-0.46,0.99,0.01,0.70,0.47,0.53,0.31,0.68,0.52,0.76,0.97,--\n\nThese e values derive from the old step 3 matrix. Note: old e(A→B) = S_old[A][B]