nMargin rank 1 − rank 2 = 0.70 ✓ unique.\n\nHmm wait, I should also double-check S_new_stomach values against all 15 columns in the script (will compute). And S_new_prostate too.\n\nAlso: CSV rank assignment: rank all 105 by swap_score descending; ties → stable order by pair tuple (fine).\n\nevidence_type column: 'promoter_accessibility+marker_coherence' for all rows; for rank 1: '+hallmark_genes'.\n\nswap_call.json:\n{\n  \"swap_detected\": true,\n  \"organ_a\": \"Cloaca\",\n  \"organ_b\": \"Stomach\",\n  \"confidence\": ~0.96,\n  \"evidence\": \"...\"\n}\nLexicographic check: 'Cloaca' < 'Stomach' ✓ (C < S).\n\nEvidence string: build from the numbers:\n- \"Column labeled Stomach shows the strongest accessibility of Cloaca marker genes (z +0.82 vs +0.13 in column Cloaca)\" — wait, direction: cloaca markers: S_cloaca[Stomach column] = +0.82 vs S_cloaca[Cloaca column] = +0.13 ✓.\n- \"Column labeled Cloaca shows the strongest accessibility of Stomach marker genes (z +0.88 vs −0.28 in column Stomach)\" ✓.\n- Hallmarks: stomach markers CLDN18 (z +3.24, column Cloaca), TFF3.2 (+2.91, Cloaca), SHH (+2.52, Cloaca); cloaca markers CDX2 (+2.34 in Stomach column), HOXC11 (+2.02), MSMB (+2.63 in Stomach column)... hmm, in analysis.py the HALLMARKS['Stomach'] list (markers that should be open in true stomach tissue, checked across columns): CLDN18, SHH, TFF3.2, MUC2, PGA3, PGC. And HALLMARKS['Cloaca'] = CDX2, HOXC11, HOXC10, MSMB, TMPRSS3, HOXB13 — hmm wait, in analysis.py I set HALLMARKS['Cloaca'] = ['CDX2','HOXC11','HOXC10','MSMB','TMPRSS3','HOXB13'] (markers of cloaca/posterior identity), HALLMARKS['Stomach'] = gastric markers. But the JSON evidence builder loops `for organ in (a, b)` and says \"hallmark genes for {organ}: ... peaks in column ...\". For organ_a=Cloaca: hallmarks CDX2/HOXC11/HOXC10/MSMB/TMPRSS3/HOXB13 — argmax columns: CDX2 → Intestine (2.35) hmm!! CDX2's argmax is Intestine not Stomach (Stomach column 2.34, tied). And MSMB's argmax → Stomach column ✓, HOXC11 